jecture100.conjecture100  | Proved by Kias Henry in August 2026; the library links his proof. Found in the open-problem sweep.\n\nNot all of these are first formal proofs. When this paper was written the library already linked proofs by other people for the Erdős 105 variant, for A112970, for the Giuga-to-Carmichael implication and for Graffiti.pc 100, and a theorem named ramsey_number_four_four exists in Bhavik Mehta’s Ramsey project, so $R(4,4)=18$ very likely has an earlier Lean proof with other definitions. The two TxGraffiti disproofs are the only ones for which I found no earlier Lean proof; the counterexample graphs are from Fischer and from the txgraffiti-order48-successor repository, and the Lean proofs add the machine check.\n\nTwo known results were not finished in their time box: Chen and Saito’s theorem that minimum degree 3 forces a cycle of length divisible by 3, and the Danzer–Klee bound ${2}^{n-1}$ for snakes in the $n$-cube. Both tasks came without a proof sketch.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n- Braß [2] seems to have been unaware that the question he posed was equivalent to tripod packing and monotone matrices (or, like us, had never heard of these problems). (https://www.combinatorics.org/ojs/index.php/eljc/article/download/v26i1p8/pdf/)\nciteturn0search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7.8 years ago; - Gowers and Long [6] arrived at 2-comparable sets as a relaxation of a problem (the size of the largest 2-increasing sequence of triples) proposed by Loh [7].\n- Braß [2] seems to have been unaware that the question he posed was equivalent to tripod packing and monotone matrices (or, like us, had never heard of these problems).\n- Tiskin [13], apparently unaware of the relation between tripod packing and induced matchings, proved an upper bound of \\(o(n^2)\\) for tripod packing. His proof does not depend on any properties of tripod packing that are not also true for induced matchings, and uses t